[2026-03-14T23:23:48.174Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014BvFg7v5U3F5aV3SHPYAc8","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Documentation\n\n## Overview\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. Users can install it, record sessions, upload recordings, and manage them through command-line commands.\n\n## Installation\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\nUsers must create an API key at https://app.replay.io settings and save it to the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `record [url]` | Launch Replay Browser and start recording a session |\n| `upload [ids...]` | Upload recordings to the Replay service |\n| `list` | View all local recordings with details |\n| `remove [ids...]` | Delete one or more recordings |\n| `login/logout` | Manage account authentication |\n| `info` | Display CLI and browser version information |\n| `upload-source-maps` | Upload source maps for a workspace |\n\n## Basic Workflow\n\n**Record a session:**\n```sh\nreplayio record https://myapp.com\n```\n\n**Upload a recording:**\n```sh\nreplayio upload <recording-id>\n```\n\n## MCP Server Integration\nThe Replay MCP Server enables debugging recorded applications within Claude by configuring it with your `REPLAY_API_KEY`.\n\nAll commands support `-h` or `--help` for additional information."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e29039f7-9bfa-4d98-aa1e-c59811d98508","uuid":"06eff4e4-11fd-46c6-9450-ed39d175cb43","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Documentation\n\n## Overview\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. Users can install it, record sessions, upload recordings, and manage them through command-line commands.\n\n## Installation\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\nUsers must create an API key at https://app.replay.io settings and save it to the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `record [url]` | Launch Replay Browser and start recording a session |\n| `upload [ids...]` | Upload recordings to the Replay service |\n| `list` | View all local recordings with details |\n| `remove [ids...]` | Delete one or more recordings |\n| `login/logout` | Manage account authentication |\n| `info` | Display CLI and browser version information |\n| `upload-source-maps` | Upload source maps for a workspace |\n\n## Basic Workflow\n\n**Record a session:**\n```sh\nreplayio record https://myapp.com\n```\n\n**Upload a recording:**\n```sh\nreplayio upload <recording-id>\n```\n\n## MCP Server Integration\nThe Replay MCP Server enables debugging recorded applications within Claude by configuring it with your `REPLAY_API_KEY`.\n\nAll commands support `-h` or `--help` for additional information.","durationMs":3257,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-14T23:23:48.410Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ct9GfrXkCNyLeKqRxNjZsU","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution data. As described, \"Replay MCP is used to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings.\"\n\n## Key Capabilities\n\nThe system provides three main tool categories:\n\n**Exploratory Tools** help discover what occurred in recordings through error detection, timeline analysis, and source code examination.\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events happened, using dependency tracking and detailed state inspection.\n\n## Investigation Methodology\n\nThe documentation emphasizes a structured approach: frame questions, identify relevant events, understand their causes, form hypotheses, and support conclusions with evidence. As stated: \"The most important thing to remember when using Replay MCP to investigate a recording is to not jump to conclusions.\"\n\n## Practical Guidance\n\nThe Logpoint tool is highlighted as particularly valuable for tracking expression values across multiple execution points, while ControlDependency helps understand event timing and causation."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e29039f7-9bfa-4d98-aa1e-c59811d98508","uuid":"09ebf034-4181-4116-a072-2e7ef44de5f9","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution data. As described, \"Replay MCP is used to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings.\"\n\n## Key Capabilities\n\nThe system provides three main tool categories:\n\n**Exploratory Tools** help discover what occurred in recordings through error detection, timeline analysis, and source code examination.\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events happened, using dependency tracking and detailed state inspection.\n\n## Investigation Methodology\n\nThe documentation emphasizes a structured approach: frame questions, identify relevant events, understand their causes, form hypotheses, and support conclusions with evidence. As stated: \"The most important thing to remember when using Replay MCP to investigate a recording is to not jump to conclusions.\"\n\n## Practical Guidance\n\nThe Logpoint tool is highlighted as particularly valuable for tracking expression values across multiple execution points, while ControlDependency helps understand event timing and causation.","durationMs":2951,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
